 "result": "I fixed `apply_discount` in `calc/pricing.py`, and `test_discount_rounding` now passes. I ran only that test after the change; I didn't re-run `test_no_discount`.\n\n**Cause:** the function used `int()`, which cuts off the decimals instead of rounding. In floating point, `2.30 * 0.5 * 100` comes out as about `114.99999\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6`, so `int()` turned it into 114 cents and the function returned `1.14` instead of `1.15`.\n\n**Fix:** the function now works out the price in cents and rounds it:\n\n```python\nreturn round(price * (100 - pct)) / 100\n```\n\n`2.30 * 50 = 115.0`, which rounds to 115 cents and returns `1.15`.\n\n**Test run:** `python -m unittest -v tests.test_pricing.TestPricing.test_discount_rounding` \u00e2\u2020\u2019 `test_discount_rounding ... ok` (1 test, OK).\n\nRounding versus truncation: before, discounted prices were always cut down to the cent below. Now they go to the nearest cent, so some other results will change too.",
